<Base title="How we test" description="The process behind every DesignTested review and comparison.">
  <h1>How we test</h1>
  <p>Every recommendation on DesignTested follows the same process, so reviews can be compared with each other.</p>
  <h2>1. We use the product</h2>
  <p>We sign up for a free trial or demo (or buy a month where there is none) and work through a standard small project: one room from first sketch to a client-ready presentation, plus a proposal and an invoice where the tool supports them.</p>
  <h2>2. We score the same things every time</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Speed to result:</strong> how long it takes to get from a blank project to something you can show a client.</li>
    <li><strong>Output quality:</strong> renders, plans, documents or proposals you can send as they are.</li>
    <li><strong>Learning curve:</strong> how much time a designer needs before the tool pays for itself.</li>
    <li><strong>Real cost:</strong> the plan you actually need, not the cheapest headline price.</li>
    <li><strong>Support and reliability:</strong> documentation, response times, and what happens when you cancel.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>3. We check facts at the source</h2>
  <p>Prices, limits and features come from the vendor&rsquo;s own pricing and help pages and are re-checked when we update an article. Every article shows its last-updated date. Software changes quickly; if you spot something out of date, please <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>.</p>
  <h2>4. We say what we could not test</h2>
  <p>When we have not used a feature ourselves, we say so instead of repeating the vendor&rsquo;s marketing.</p>
</Base>
